id: smemstat-0.02.13-make-cli-cflags-override
error_signature: use of undeclared identifier 'VERSION' (define missing entirely) | invalid suffix '[0-9.]+' on floating constant (define re-supplied but quoting stripped by shell layers)
match_keywords: CFLAGS,command line,override,+=,plus-equals,-DVERSION,VERSION,undefined identifier,floating constant,Makefile,append
category: build-system,make,conan-recipe
severity: 2
trigger_tool: make|cc|clang
phase: build
keywords: CFLAGS, make, command line, override, append, plus-equals, VERSION, define, quoting, direct make recipe
root_cause: Plain-Makefile projects carry per-project flags in an append (e.g. CFLAGS += -Wall -Wextra -DVERSION='"$(VERSION)"' -O2 -g); a recipe that builds with an explicit command-line assignment (make CFLAGS=...) silently DEACTIVATES every += append because GNU make gives command-line variables highest priority and a makefile += on a command-line variable is ignored (unlike an environment variable where += still appends), so upstream defines are lost with two compile-time faces both reproduced on smemstat 0.02.13 (clang 15 / OHOS aarch64): (a) define missing entirely -> "use of undeclared identifier 'VERSION'"; (b) define re-supplied but quoting stripped by one of the two shell layers (invocation shell, then make recipe expansion) so the bare token reaches the compiler -> "invalid suffix '.13' on floating constant".
rec_approach: resupply-full-cflags-with-quoted-version-define
rec_description: Supply the COMPLETE flag set on the make command line (document in the recipe that the Makefile's += appends are inactive) and re-add upstream defines in the upstream quoting form so double quotes survive both shell expansions to the compiler: the CFLAGS value must literally contain -DVERSION='"X.Y.Z"' (single quotes eaten by the invocation shell, double quotes eaten by the recipe shell, leaving a C string literal). Build the assignment with shlex.quote() so shell metacharacters in include/lib paths cannot split the argument. Passing CFLAGS via the environment instead would preserve += appends, but the explicit command-line form is deterministic and keeps R33 compliance (no reliance on ambient shell variables).
rec_commands: make -C <src> -j2 CC="<profile clang>" CFLAGS=<shlex.quote(f"-O2 -fPIC -DVERSION='\"{version}\"' -I{dep_inc}")> LDFLAGS=<shlex.quote(f"-L{dep_lib}")> smemstat
verification: smemstat/0.02.13 on ohos-aarch64: conan create green (G2), package verified (G1-G4, L2 smoke executable, L4/L5), consumer test_package 3/3 PASS; negative cases reproduced with the exact signatures above and the positive build only succeeds with the fully resupplied CFLAGS including the quoted -DVERSION define.
related: archives/s/smemstat/0.02.13/conanfile.py (working recipe) | archives/d/dhcpoptinj/0.5.3/conanfile.py (direct-compile precedent with the same quoting form) | knowledge/graph/E063.kv (CFLAGS -Werror specific, distinct failure)
last_updated: 2026-09-18
